Discover and test exact cloud request identifiers.
A local model tag does not prove cloud availability.

ARCHITECTURE
Use a frontend plus a secure server/API layer.
Use a durable job mechanism when asynchronous work requires it.
Choose hosting based on verified capabilities.

Separate:
- Domain models and mutations.
- Authorization.
- Persistence.
- Provider adapters.
- Jobs.
- Usage accounting.
- Rendering.
- UI.

Never force Python FastAPI into a host that cannot run it.
If using the supplied stock endpoint, either deploy FastAPI
appropriately or port its behavior into the chosen backend.

GLOBAL RULES
- Provider secrets stay server-side.
- Authenticate and authorize before billable work.
- No mock content behind a working-looking generation button.
- No automatic external deployment, resource creation, or purchases.
- Preserve original media.
- Respect locks in domain/server logic.
- Snapshot generation and render inputs.
- Detect staleness using content fingerprints.
- Preserve bounded recoverable history.
- Use migrations and stable IDs.
- Validate provider output independently.
- Bound retries and concurrency.
- Never claim provider cancellation guarantees no charge.
- Never promise factual verification or guaranteed ad performance.
- Clearly distinguish storyboard previews from rendered video.

PHASE REPORT
For each acceptance criterion report:
PASS, FAIL, or UNVERIFIED.

Separate:
- Mocked tests.
- Live provider calls.
- In-app browser checks.
- Exported-file inspection.

Report dependencies, migrations, configuration requirements,
cost assumptions, security limitations, and remaining blockers.

Stop after the requested phase.
